# TravelCore — Architecture Rules (Locked)

## Stack (do not change)
- .NET 10, ASP.NET Core Minimal API
- Next.js 16, React 19
- PostgreSQL, Redis
- Modular Monolith + Clean Architecture
- MediatR **12.5.0** (do not upgrade to 13+; commercial)
- MassTransit **8.5.12** (do not upgrade to 9+; commercial)
- Languages: FA (default), EN, AR

## Module layout (mandatory)
Every module has exactly four projects:
`Domain`, `Application`, `Infrastructure`, `Presentation`.

- Domain: entities, value objects, domain events, invariants. No external dependencies.
- Application: Commands/, Queries/, Validators, Ports, DTOs. No EF/HTTP.
- Infrastructure: EF Core, migrations, repositories, adapters.
- Presentation: Minimal API endpoints, contracts, filters.

## Hard rules
- No project reference between modules. Use `TravelCore.Contracts.*` only.
- No cross-schema SQL joins.
- One Command/Query per folder with Handler + Validator.
- Commands mutate; Queries use read models.
- All money as minor units + currency.
- All POST payment/booking endpoints require `Idempotency-Key`.
- Publish integration events through Outbox only.
- Cache access only via `ICacheService`.
- Messaging only via `IIntegrationEventPublisher` (or MassTransit contracts in Infrastructure).
- No `Helper`, `Manager`, `Utils`, generic `Service` classes.
- No secrets in code or appsettings committed.
- No PII in logs; use redaction.

## Three API surfaces (never mix DTOs)
- `/supplier/v1` — agency ingests offers/departures/availability.
- `/channel/v1` — agency sells authorized offers.
- `/market/v1` — consumer marketplace; plus Next.js BFF.

## Money (locked)
- Agency is Merchant of Record. TravelCore never holds customer funds.
- Payments go to the agency PSP account (`MerchantScope = Agency`).
- Commission/subscription is invoiced to the agency (monthly, dunning, credit limit).
- No PSP/intermediary logic in TravelCore.

## Plans (locked)
- Standard: `Powered by TravelCore` required, no white-label.
- Professional: full white-label, higher subscription.
- Entitlements are the source of truth (`whiteLabel`, `attributionRequired`, limits, commissionRate, seoCanonicalMode).
- Never enable Professional features without an active entitlement.

## Flights (locked)
- Separate `Flights` module/schema.
- Supplier adapter pattern + Mock; inventory is supplier-owned.
- Flow: Search → Quote → PNR → Payment → Ticketing → Refund.
- PNR/Ticket/Refund idempotent; ticketing deadline job mandatory.
- Never issue ticket without confirmed payment.

## SEO (locked)
- SEO is a workstream from phase 0, not a final phase.
- Server Components + ISR; one canonical per product/route.
- Offer/facet/date pages: noindex or canonical to product/route.
- Channel Standard canonical → TravelCore; Professional → agency/self only with unique content.
- Slug changes require 301; per-locale sitemap and hreflang.

## Tour model (locked)
- `TourProduct` is shared and platform-owned.
- `AgencyOffer` is tenant-owned and references `TourProduct`.
- `TourDeparture` belongs to `AgencyOffer`.
- Price/capacity/cancellation live on Offer/Departure.
- Snapshot Offer + Departure at booking time.

## Observability
- Serilog + OpenTelemetry.
- Toggles: `Observability:Logging/Tracing/Metrics:Enabled` and per-module overrides.
- Enrich: TraceId, SpanId, TenantId, AgencyId, UserId, Module.
- Audit log is separate and always on.

## Database
- Schema per module.
- `uuid` (UUIDv7) ids, `timestamptz`, `jsonb` for localized text.
- Each module owns its `DbContext` and migrations.
- `tenant_id` on agency-owned tables; enforce via `TenantContext`.

## i18n / SEO
- Locales: fa, en, ar with `[locale]` route segment.
- `dir` switches rtl/ltr.
- LocalizedText for content fields.
- Per-locale slug, canonical, hreflang, sitemap.

## Workflow
- Small tasks only (<= 1 day).
- Update `PLAN.md` / ADR before architectural changes.
- Run architecture tests before commit.
- Commit format: `feat(module): ...`.
